{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01Ao4vpahLRRLPFJs9eMEHsr","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Let me analyze the research context carefully to define three tiers (best/median/worst) for the Dream simulation.\n\nKey facts from the project:\n1. This is an IRT person-fit contamination detection paper targeting EMNLP 2026\n2. Core method: using IRT lz* statistic on binary response patterns to detect benchmark contamination\n3. Completed experiments: simulation (power 97.9% MMLU@15%), empirical null (well-calibrated), ctrl-contam pilot (Qwen2.5-7B, |d|=3.85 at 15%), 4PL ablation, domain analysis, etc.\n\n\n4. Still ahead: the full ctrl-contam experiment across multiple models and benchmarks, a Qwen3.5-9B variant, baseline comparisons, and post-RL analysis\n\nThe real question is whether the method generalizes beyond the initial Qwen2.5-7B results—can it detect contamination consistently across different model families and on smaller benchmarks like GSM8K and HellaSwag, and does lz* actually outperform existing baselines?\n\nLooking at the pilot data from Qwen2.5-7B on MMLU, the effect sizes are strong: Cohen's d hits 3.85 at 15% contamination with a dose-response ratio of 2.93, memorization sits at 38%, and the seen/unseen split is dramatic (lz* near zero for seen items versus 3.1 for unseen). The key metrics I need to track across all experiments are Cohen's d consistency, how many models show significant detection, the range of memorization fractions, and whether the θ-shift problem scales with model size.\n\nNow I'm defining success tiers based on how robust these findings are. Best case: all four models show consistent strong detection across benchmarks, post-RL signal holds up, and lz* stays competitive with baselines even at low contamination. Median case: detection works on most model families but some benchmarks are too small, θ-shift needs careful mitigation, post-RL partially degrades the signal, and certain baselines win at specific operating points. Worst case: detection only reliable on one or two model families, small benchmarks fail entirely, θ-shift becomes severe and uncontrollable, post-RL destroys the signal—though the universal misfit finding and theoretical framework still contribute value.\n\nI'm setting numerical targets now: for Cohen's d across the four models at 15% contamination, I want to see how many hit the strong effect size threshold. Looking at the signal retention patterns across post-RL scenarios and how they vary by benchmark size, with MMLU's larger dataset providing stronger statistical power than GSM8K's smaller one. The key narratives are shaping up around whether IRT-FIT functions as a minimal-information contamination detector that generalizes across model families and remains robust to fine-tuning, or whether its effectiveness is more limited to specific benchmarks and conditions.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":20446,"cache_read_input_tokens":11841,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":20446},"output_tokens":18,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c0112abd-a6eb-400a-a707-22e026da7bd9","uuid":"05a5616d-09ab-4d7b-a1df-16c48ef81681"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01Ao4vpahLRRLPFJs9eMEHsr","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"```yaml\ntiers:\n  best:\n    meaning: \"Multi-model ctrl-contam 全面成功 + post-RL 信号存活 + lz* 在低污染率胜出所有 baselines\"\n    key_assumptions:\n      - \"SFT memorization fingerprint跨模型家族一致：4/4 模型在 15% 污染下均产生显著 Δlz*\"\n      - \"θ-fixed 策略普适：所有模型均可通过固定 θ 恢复单调 dose-response\"\n      - \"Post-RL 不破坏 binary response 层面的记忆痕迹（GRPO 后 Δlz* 保留 ≥70%）\"\n      - \"小 benchmark（GSM8K ~1.3K items）在 ctrl-contam 中仍产生可检测信号（|d| > 0.8）\"\n      - \"lz* 在 5-10% 低污染率下 AUROC 持续优于所有 supervised baselines\"\n    number_ranges:\n      cohens_d_15pct_across_models: [2.0, 5.0]  # median across 4 models\n      cohens_d_15pct_min_model: [1.5, 3.0]  # worst-performing model\n      models_significant_at_15pct: [4, 4]  # out of 4\n      benchmarks_significant_per_model: [2, 3]  # out of 3 (MMLU+HellaSwag+GSM8K)\n      memorization_fraction_15pct: [0.30, 0.50]\n      theta_fixed_dose_response_ratio: [2.5, 4.0]  # contam_50/contam_15\n      post_rl_signal_retention: [0.70, 1.00]  # Δlz* post-GRPO / Δlz* post-SFT\n      lz_star_auroc_5pct: [0.70, 0.85]\n      lz_star_auroc_10pct: [0.80, 0.92]\n      lz_star_minus_best_baseline_auroc_5pct: [0.00, 0.15]  # lz* advantage\n      seen_unseen_lz_gap_15pct: [2.5, 5.0]\n    narrative_direction: >\n      原始 framing 完全成立。IRT-FIT 是 minimal-information operating point 上的有效检测框架：\n      跨 4 个模型家族一致检测、post-RL robust、在实际关键的低污染率下无需标注数据即胜过 supervised baselines。\n      三条 claims 无需调整——Claim 1 的 \"principled framework\" 有 ctrl-contam 全面验证，\n      Claim 2 的 power function 有 multi-benchmark 实证确认，Claim 3 的 empirical findings\n      加入 ctrl-contam 的跨模型 memorization 量化。θ-shift 作为 methodological contribution 而非 limitation。\n      Headline: \"binary response patterns alone detect SFT contamination across model families,\n      even after RL post-training.\"\n\n  median:\n    meaning: \"MMLU 上检测跨模型可靠，但小 benchmark 或个别模型家族失败；post-RL 部分降级；baselines 在某些 operating points 胜出\"\n    key_assumptions:\n      - \"3/4 模型在 MMLU 15% 污染下显著，但 1 个模型家族（如 Mistral）memorization fraction 过低导致信号不足\"\n      - \"GSM8K（1.3K items）在多数模型上 |d| < 0.8，power 不足——与理论预测一致但限制实用性\"\n      - \"θ-fixed 在 3/4 模型上恢复单调性，1 个模型出现非标准 θ-shift pattern\"\n      - \"Post-RL 信号衰减 40-70%——person-fit 未完全失效但 effect size 大幅缩水\"\n      - \"lz* 在 5% 污染时与 best baseline 持平或略优，10%+ 时 ML baselines 追上\"\n    number_ranges:\n      cohens_d_15pct_across_models: [1.0, 3.0]\n      cohens_d_15pct_min_model: [0.5, 1.5]\n      models_significant_at_15pct: [3, 4]  # 3-4 out of 4 on MMLU\n      benchmarks_significant_per_model: [1, 2]  # mostly MMLU, sometimes HellaSwag\n      memorization_fraction_15pct: [0.15, 0.35]\n      theta_fixed_dose_response_ratio: [1.5, 3.0]\n      post_rl_signal_retention: [0.30, 0.70]\n      lz_star_auroc_5pct: [0.58, 0.72]\n      lz_star_auroc_10pct: [0.65, 0.80]\n      lz_star_minus_best_baseline_auroc_5pct: [-0.05, 0.05]  # roughly tied\n      seen_unseen_lz_gap_15pct: [1.0, 3.0]\n    narrative_direction: >\n      需要将 claims 从 \"detection framework\" 调整为 \"detection characterization framework with\n      quantified operating conditions\"。Claim 1 调整为：lz* 在大 benchmark（≥10K items）上提供可靠检测，\n      并量化检测力随 benchmark size 和 model architecture 的变化——operating conditions 本身是贡献。\n      Claim 2 不变（power function 已是理论贡献）。Claim 3 增加 ctrl-contam 跨模型异质性分析：\n      不同模型家族的 memorization fraction 差异反映 SFT generalization 的架构依赖性。\n      Post-RL 结果如果衰减但非归零，framing 为 \"partially robust, more robust than log-prob methods\n      (which completely fail per Wang et al.)\"。补充实验：可能需要增加一个 model 或 benchmark 以补强。\n      Headline 调整为 \"IRT-FIT characterizes the detection frontier at the minimal-information\n      operating point, with quantified power under varying contamination, benchmark, and\n      post-training conditions.\"\n\n  worst:\n    meaning: \"ctrl-contam 仅在原始 pilot 条件（Qwen × MMLU）可复现，跨模型/benchmark 泛化失败；post-RL 信号消失；baselines 多数场景胜出\"\n    key_assumptions:\n      - \"仅 1-2/4 模型在 MMLU 15% 下显著——SFT generalization 在多数模型上将 memorization fraction 压到 <15%\"\n      - \"θ-shift 机制在某些模型上不可控：θ-fixed 也无法恢复单调 dose-response\"\n      - \"Post-RL 完全消除 person-fit 信号（retention <30%），与 MIA 方法一样失效\"\n      - \"ML baselines 在 10%+ 全面胜出 lz*，lz* 仅在极低污染率（3-5%）有微弱优势但 AUROC < 0.65 无实用价值\"\n      - \"Universal 4PL misfit、θ-shift mechanism、seen/unseen fingerprint 等发现仍成立但检测实用性不足\"\n    number_ranges:\n      cohens_d_15pct_across_models: [0.3, 1.5]\n      cohens_d_15pct_min_model: [0.1, 0.5]\n      models_significant_at_15pct: [1, 2]\n      benchmarks_significant_per_model: [1, 1]  # MMLU only, and not all models\n      memorization_fraction_15pct: [0.05, 0.20]\n      theta_fixed_dose_response_ratio: [0.8, 2.0]  # near 1.0 = no dose-response\n      post_rl_signal_retention: [0.00, 0.30]\n      lz_star_auroc_5pct: [0.50, 0.62]\n      lz_star_auroc_10pct: [0.55, 0.70]\n      lz_star_minus_best_baseline_auroc_5pct: [-0.15, -0.03]  # lz* loses\n      seen_unseen_lz_gap_15pct: [0.3, 1.5]\n    narrative_direction: >\n      核心 reframe：从 \"contamination detection method\" 转向 \"psychometric diagnostics for\n      LLM evaluation\"。三条 claims 重构——\n      Claim 1 变为：IRT person-fit 为 LLM benchmark 评估提供 principled diagnostic 工具，\n      ctrl-contam 的 pilot 成功 + full 失败共同量化了 binary-only detection 的 fundamental limits\n      （这本身是对 detection frontier 的贡献：我们精确度量了 minimal-information operating point 的天花板）。\n      Claim 2 保留 power function 理论贡献，但增加 \"adjusted power after SFT generalization\" 的\n      empirical bound，展示理论上限与实际信号的 gap 作为 SFT generalization 量化。\n      Claim 3 的重心转移到三个 standalone 发现：(a) universal 4PL misfit 作为 LLM response pattern\n      的结构性发现（所有 LLM 都不是 classical test-takers），(b) θ-shift mechanism 作为 person-fit\n      在 adaptive testing 场景中的 methodological warning，(c) memorization fraction 的跨模型\n      异质性揭示 SFT generalization 的本质。\n      仍冲 EMNLP——venue fit 从 \"evaluation methodology\" 转为 \"empirical analysis of LLM\n      evaluation assumptions\"，类似 \"Are LLMs classical test-takers? Evidence from IRT\n      person-fit analysis\" 的 empirical study framing。不降级目标。\n```"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":20446,"cache_read_input_tokens":11841,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":20446},"output_tokens":18,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c0112abd-a6eb-400a-a707-22e026da7bd9","uuid":"ebd99d1e-8355-455b-a4f7-d0b40329d966"}
